  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 207 AM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nBy Sunday the cold front begins to slip in far northern Iowa \nwith highs there in the upper 50s to low 60s on Sunday. \nMeanwhile most of Iowa will be in the mid 70s once again on \nSunday. A few isolated showers are possible in northern Iowa on \nSunday, however dry air will mitigate most development. As the \ncutoff low across the southwest US finally lifts into the \nmidwest Monday into Tuesday moisture increases and will allow \nfor spotty showers across the area. The cool front finally sinks\nacross the area bringing temperatures down into the 60s. There \nwill be a brief respite with weak mid-level ridging before the \nstronger trough from the Pacific Northwest swings through our \nregion in the middle to end of next week. That system will push \na stronger surface trough through and sweep out most remaining \nmoisture from the earlier systems, bringing quieter autumn \nweather for at least a couple of days afterward in the extended \nforecast.",
